cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "QPDK: Superconducting Quantum Process Design Kit"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23698129
message: >-
  If you use QPDK in research, please cite the Zenodo record for the release
  you used. Use the concept DOI when referring to the project as a whole.
  See the README for citation guidance.
abstract: >-
  QPDK is an open-source process design kit for superconducting quantum RF
  circuits, built on gdsfactory. It provides parametric layout components
  including qubits, Josephson junctions, resonators, capacitors, and couplers,
  with coplanar waveguide routing, layer stacks, and KLayout technology files.
  Analytical circuit models use SAX and JAX for differentiable S-parameter
  simulation. Test-chip examples, finite element datasets, and worked
  notebooks connect layout design to circuit, quantum, and electromagnetic
  simulation, parameter extraction, and optimization.
